# broiler-js-conformance retained suite pin 1
#
# The shared conformance vectors of the shared JavaScript libraries programme (milestone SJL-1): a
# corpus whose home is the Broiler.JS repository, retained here as the archive of one named corpus
# revision. `revision` is the Broiler.JS commit that carries it, an immutable commit and never a
# branch name, and the corpus at that commit is at corpus revision 16 (its REVISIONS.md).
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. On 2026-10-15, with `git archive` of that commit, twice, into two files: the two
# were byte-identical. The second was extracted into a fresh directory and its files hashed there,
# independently of the in-memory reading the harness makes, which is what makes `content-sha256` a
# reading rather than a copy of an earlier one. The command, which anybody with the Broiler.JS
# repository can repeat:
#
#   git archive --format=tar.gz <revision> -- conformance/vectors ':(exclude)conformance/vectors/controls'
#
# WHAT IS HERE. One file of 971,983 bytes hashing to `archive-sha256`, which extracts to the 37
# files `content-sha256` is over: the number area's ten vector files, the numerics area's eight, the
# text area's six, the Date area's seven, the schema, the README, the revision log, the prelude and
# the two source pins. The negative controls stay in Broiler.JS; the home's validator is the one that
# reads them.
#
# HOW IT IS READ. `--vectors <archive> --expect <this file>` of the conformance root checks both
# digests and the count before any vector runs. `content-sha256` is over the files' paths below
# conformance/vectors/ and their SHA-256 digests, sorted, as `<path> LF <digest> LF` lines - the
# digest every retained suite pin in this repository uses.
#
# REVISIONS OF THIS PIN. Taken at corpus revision 3 (Broiler.JS 593f2c5bce1f055025864af2b7ec38ee6f2f835a)
# on 2026-10-12, at milestone SJL-1; moved to revision 7 on 2026-10-13, at milestone SJL-4.2, which
# adds the numerics area and retires the 391 divergence fields this profile's SJL-3.4 cut-over
# corrected. Its header read, for the first pin: "the corpus at that commit is at corpus revision 3",
# "On 2026-10-12" and "One file of 305,816 bytes hashing to `archive-sha256`, which extracts to the 16
# files `content-sha256` is over: the number area's ten vector files, the schema, the README, the
# revision log, the prelude and the two source pins." Moved to revision 9 on 2026-10-14, at milestone
# SJL-4.6, which retires every divergence field of the numerics area: this profile's, which its SJL-4.4
# cut-over corrected, and Broiler.JS's, which its SJL-4.5 cut-over corrected. Its header read, for
# revision 7: "the corpus at that commit is at corpus revision 7", "On 2026-10-13" and "One file of
# 578,788 bytes hashing to `archive-sha256`"; the number of files did not change. Moved to revision 12
# on 2026-10-14, at milestone SJL-5.2: revision 10 adds the text area, revision 11 widens the schema's
# clause ids, and revision 12 classifies both engines' first runs on the area, this profile's five
# differences among them, which its SJL-5.4 cut-over corrects. Its header read, for revision 9: "the
# corpus at that commit is at corpus revision 9" and "One file of 588,023 bytes hashing to
# `archive-sha256`, which extracts to the 24 files `content-sha256` is over: the number area's ten
# vector files, the numerics area's eight, the schema, the README, the revision log, the prelude and
# the two source pins." Moved to revision 13 on 2026-10-15, at milestones SJL-5.4 and SJL-5.5, which
# retires every divergence field of the text area: this profile's five, which its SJL-5.4 cut-over
# corrected, and Broiler.JS's 42, which its SJL-5.5 cut-over corrected. Its header read, for revision
# 12: "the corpus at that commit is at corpus revision 12", "On 2026-10-14" and "One file of 824,087
# bytes hashing to `archive-sha256`"; the number of files did not change. Moved to revision 15 on
# 2026-10-15, at milestone SJL-6.2: revision 14 adds the Date area, and revision 15 classifies both
# engines' first runs on it, this profile's sixteen differences among them, which its SJL-6.4 cut-over
# corrects. Its header read, for revision 13: "the corpus at that commit is at corpus revision 13" and
# "One file of 821,813 bytes hashing to `archive-sha256`, which extracts to the 30 files
# `content-sha256` is over: the number area's ten vector files, the numerics area's eight, the text
# area's six, the schema, the README, the revision log, the prelude and the two source pins." Moved to
# revision 16 on 2026-10-15, at milestone SJL-6.4, this profile's cut-over of the Date area: revision 16
# adds twelve implementation-defined Date vectors of strings outside the Date Time String Format, whose
# expectation for this profile is its dialect as the shared library ports it, and keeps the sixteen
# divergence fields of revision 15 that the cut-over corrects, which a run on this pin reports as no
# longer holding. Its header read, for revision 15: "the corpus at that commit is at corpus revision
# 15" and "One file of 970,459 bytes hashing to `archive-sha256`"; the number of files did not change.

